( Read an M-code handler's result back the way a real program does: from the )
( block after the call, inside a subroutine, so the interpreter has to stop )
( reading ahead at the M-code's INTERP_EXECUTE_FINISH, drain, and only then )
( fetch #5399. The MDI-only case in test.sh cannot catch a broken drain, )
( because each MDI line is its own interpreter invocation. )
o<m103check> sub
  M103
  (debug, sub-udr=#5399)
o<m103check> endsub
m2
